agm-0970: AGM H6 drop box (bsd/dev/agm_dropbox.c): files for the iOS root written from Android
into iosroot at 32 GiB (agm-h6/tools/agm-drop.py: header AGMDROP1, generation, up to 31 entries
with an FNV-1a 64 hash each) are written into place by a kernel thread once the root is
writable, once per generation (/usr/lib/agm-drop.gen); boot-arg agm_drop=0: left alone.
And the display waits for the Mali to be done with a surface and drops what the processors'
caches hold of it before showing it (RedwoodGPU.cpp topaz_surface_drawn() on AGM).

